    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0409" n="303" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg303"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Rockhill to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-01-15"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 197.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 172 of December 18
                    last, with regard to the danger to navigation in the Gulf of Pechili resulting
                    from the presence of floating mines, I have the honor to inclose a translation
                    of a note recently sent by the foreign office to the doyen of the diplomatic
                    corps, showing the steps taken by the Chinese Government to remedy this
                    evil.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
